#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:125
msgid ""
"理想気体の列は :eq:`eq-gas-ideal` による値です。\\ MD平均の列は、\\ :numref:`fig-argon-"
"pressure-time`\\ のような時系列からシードごとに時間平均を求め、3つのシードで平均した値です。\\ "
"シードとは乱数列を生成するための初期値です。\\ 標準誤差は、時間相関を考慮したブロック平均とシード間のばらつきから求めています。\\ "
"この誤差には、原子間相互作用のモデルや粒子数の有限性による偏りは含めていません。"
msgstr ""
"The ideal gas column gives values from Equation :eq:`eq-gas-ideal`. \\ "
"For the MD mean, we first computed a time average for each seed using "
"time series like the one in \\ :numref:`fig-argon-pressure-time`\\ . We "
"then averaged those values across all three seeds. \\ A seed is the "
"initial value used to generate a sequence of random numbers. \\ The "
"standard error accounts for variation across seeds and uses block "
"averaging to account for time correlations. \\ It excludes biases due to "
"the model for interatomic interactions or the finite number of particles."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:132
msgid "圧力の時間変化"
msgstr "Pressure over Time"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:134
msgid ""
"圧力はどの時刻でも同じ値になるわけではありません。\\ 試験計算の圧力と温度の変化を :numref:`fig-argon-pressure-"
"time` に示します。\\ この希薄な条件では、圧力の揺らぎの主な原因は温度、つまり運動エネルギーの揺らぎです。\\ 測定温度の標準偏差は約7 "
"K（約2.6%）で、瞬間圧力の相対的な幅と同程度です。\\ そこで、最初の40 psを除いた測定区間について平均を取ります。"
msgstr ""
"The pressure varies over time. \\ The pressure and temperature from a "
"test calculation are shown in :numref:`fig-argon-pressure-time`. \\ At "
"this low density, pressure fluctuations mainly come from fluctuations in "
"temperature, and thus in kinetic energy. \\ The measured temperature has "
"a standard deviation of about 7 K (approximately 2.6%), comparable to the"
" relative spread of the instantaneous pressure. \\ We therefore average "
"over the production period, excluding the first 40 ps."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:145
msgid ""
"一辺33.3879144 nm、シード1101の計算です。\\ 上段はEDRから0.1 ps間隔で抽出した圧力（薄線）と10 "
"psの移動平均（青線）、\\ 下段は温度です。横軸は時間（ps）、縦軸はそれぞれbar、Kです。\\ 黄色の0〜40 "
"psは平均から除いた区間です。\\ 破線は上段が独立に計算した理想気体の圧力、下段が273.15 Kです。"
msgstr ""
"The cell is 33.3879144 nm on a side and the seed is 1101. \\ The top "
"panel shows pressure sampled from the EDR every 0.1 ps (light line) and "
"its 10 ps moving mean (blue line). \\ The bottom panel shows temperature."
" The horizontal axis shows time (ps), and the vertical axes use bar and "
"K, respectively. \\ The yellow region from 0 to 40 ps is excluded from "
"the average. \\ The dashed lines mark the independently calculated ideal "
"gas pressure above and 273.15 K below."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:151
msgid ""
"このシードでは、測定区間の平均圧力は1.01192 bar、ブロック平均による標準誤差は約0.00066 barでした。\\ ブロックを5〜80 "
"psに変えたときの標準誤差を調べ、最大の値を採用しています。\\ "
"これは今回の区間で見積もった統計精度であり、あらゆる系統誤差がなくなったことを意味しません。"
msgstr ""
"For this seed, the mean pressure over the production period was 1.01192 "
"bar, with a standard error of about 0.00066 bar from block averaging. \\ "
"We checked block lengths from 5 to 80 ps and took the largest standard "
"error. \\ This estimate describes the statistical precision over the "
"interval. Systematic errors may still be present."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:156
msgid "1気圧に対応するモル体積"
msgstr "Molar Volume at 1 atm"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:158
msgid ""
"各体積の測定値を :numref:`fig-argon-pv` に示します。\\ "
"体積を小さくすると圧力が上がり、全体として理想気体の曲線に近い関係になっています。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`fig-argon-pv` shows the measurements at each volume. \\ Pressure"
" rises as volume decreases, and the overall relationship closely follows "
"the ideal gas curve."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:166
msgid ""
"上段の横軸は1 mol換算の体積（L/mol）、縦軸は圧力（bar）です。\\ 点と誤差棒は :numref:`tab-argon-pv` "
"と同じMD平均と1標準誤差、黒線は式 :eq:`eq-gas-ideal` の予測です。\\ 水平破線は1 atm＝1.01325 "
"bar、点線は一辺30、33、33.3879144、36 nmの測定値に対する近傍フィットです。\\ 誤差棒は点より小さい場合があります。\\ "
"下段は逆モル体積（mol/L）と圧縮因子Z＝PVm/(RT)です。\\ "
"黒線は理想気体、灰破線は全体の重心運動の除去だけを考えた予測、緑点線はさらに打ち切りLJの二体相互作用を加えた273.15 Kの予測です。\\ "
"橙の×印は各体積の実測平均温度へ補正した予測です。パラメータをMD圧力に合わせて決めてはいません。"
msgstr ""
"The top panel shows molar volume (L/mol) on the horizontal axis and "
"pressure (bar) on the vertical axis. \\ The points and error bars show "
"the MD means and one standard error, as in :numref:`tab-argon-pv`. The "
"black curve is the prediction from Equation :eq:`eq-gas-ideal`. \\ The "
"horizontal dashed line marks 1 atm = 1.01325 bar, and the dotted curve is"
" the local fit to measurements for side lengths of 30, 33, 33.3879144, "
"and 36 nm. \\ The error bars can be smaller than the markers. \\ The "
"bottom panel shows inverse molar volume (mol/L) and the compressibility "
"factor Z = PVm/(RT). \\ The black line is the ideal gas prediction. The "
"gray dashed line accounts only for removal of the motion of the system’s "
"center of mass, and the green dotted curve also accounts for truncated LJ"
" pair interactions at 273.15 K. \\ The orange crosses mark predictions "
"corrected to the measured mean temperature at each volume. We did not fit"
" the parameters to the MD pressures."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:174
msgid ""
"1 atmは1 barと少し違い、1.01325 barです。\\ この圧力付近の4体積の測定値に :math:`P=a/V_m+b` "
"を当てはめ、係数を自由に決めました。\\ 22.4 Lという値はフィットに使っていません。\\ 得られた1 atmのモル体積は **22.383 "
"± 0.012 L/mol** です。\\ ±は統計的なフィットの1標準誤差です。\\ 推定法と共分散は配布データの "
"``pv_fit.json`` に保存しています。"
msgstr ""
"One atmosphere differs slightly from 1 bar and equals 1.01325 bar. \\ We "
"fitted :math:`P=a/V_m+b` to the measurements at four volumes near this "
"pressure, with both coefficients free. \\ The fit did not use the value "
"22.4 L. \\ The resulting molar volume at 1 atm is **22.383 ± 0.012 "
"L/mol**. \\ The uncertainty after ± is one statistical standard error of "
"the fit. \\ The estimation method and covariance are in ``pv_fit.json`` "
"in the downloadable data."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:181
msgid "一方、理想気体の予測は次の値です。"
msgstr "The ideal gas prediction, by comparison, is"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:183
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"V_m&=\\frac{RT}{P}=22.413969545\\ \\mathrm{L/mol},\\\\\n"
"T&=273.15\\ \\mathrm{K},\\quad P=101325\\ \\mathrm{Pa}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"V_m&=\\frac{RT}{P}=22.413969545\\ \\mathrm{L/mol},\\\\\n"
"T&=273.15\\ \\mathrm{K},\\quad P=101325\\ \\mathrm{Pa}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:190
msgid ""
"MDの推定は理想値より約0.14%小さく、どちらも有効数字3桁では約22.4 L/molになります。\\ "
"この差は、主に二つの効果で説明できます。\\ "
"一つは全体の重心運動を取り除く効果で、原子1,000個では運動による圧力が約0.10%小さくなります。\\ "
"もう一つは今回の打ち切りLJモデルの引力で、理想気体に近い密度での独立な見積もりでは、圧力を約0.07%下げます。\\ "
"平均温度が指定値より約0.07 K高かった効果（約+0.02%）も合わせると、約−0.15%の予測になります。\\ "
"6体積の各測定値とこの予測との差は、いずれも統計標準誤差の0.5倍以内でした。\\ 見積もりの式と数値積分は "
":doc:`reproduction` にまとめています。\\ "
"この一致は今回の有限個の粒子と相互作用モデルについての確認であり、実在Arの状態方程式を高精度に決めたという意味ではありません。"
msgstr ""
"The MD estimate is about 0.14% below the ideal value. Both round to about"
" 22.4 L/mol to three significant figures. \\ Two effects account for most"
" of the difference. \\ First, removing the motion of the system’s center "
"of mass reduces the kinetic contribution to pressure by about 0.10% for "
"1,000 atoms. \\ Second, an independent estimate for the truncated LJ "
"model at densities close to those of an ideal gas gives a pressure "
"reduction of about 0.07% from attraction. \\ Including the effect of the "
"mean temperature being about 0.07 K above the target (about +0.02%) gives"
" a predicted pressure deviation of about −0.15%. \\ At all six volumes, "
"the measured pressure was within 0.5 statistical standard errors of the "
"prediction. \\ The equations and numerical integration are described in "
":doc:`reproduction`. \\ This agreement is a check only for the finite "
"number of particles and the interaction model used here. It does not "
"establish a high-precision equation of state for real Ar."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:199
msgid "原子1,000個のセルの体積は、次の式で1 molあたりへ換算しました。"
msgstr "We converted the volume of the 1,000-atom cell to volume per mole using"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:201
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"V_m[\\mathrm{L/mol}]\n"
"&=\\frac{N_A}{1000}V_{\\mathrm{box}}[\\mathrm{nm^3}]\\times10^{-24}\\\\\n"
"&=0.000602214076\\,V_{\\mathrm{box}}[\\mathrm{nm^3}].\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"V_m[\\mathrm{L/mol}]\n"
