"&=0.000602214076\\,V_{\\mathrm{box}}[\\mathrm{nm^3}].\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:210
msgid "原子の運動と圧力"
msgstr "Atomic Motion and Pressure"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:212
msgid ""
"GROMACSは、原子の運動エネルギーと原子間力から圧力を計算します [1]_ 。\\ "
"温度を一定に保つと運動エネルギーの平均が決まるので、運動による部分は理想気体の式と同じ形になります。\\ "
"ここで調べたのは、原子間力による部分がどのくらい小さいかです。\\ 1 "
"atm付近では約0.07%、今回の体積の範囲では約0.04〜0.13%だけ圧力を下げる寄与でした。"
msgstr ""
"GROMACS calculates pressure from the atoms’ kinetic energy and "
"interatomic forces [1]_. \\ At constant temperature, the mean kinetic "
"energy is fixed, so the kinetic contribution has the same form as in the "
"ideal gas equation. \\ We examined how small the contribution from "
"interatomic forces is. \\ These forces reduced the pressure by about "
"0.07% near 1 atm and by about 0.04–0.13% over the range of volumes we "
"examined."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:217
msgid ""
"22.4 Lは、原子1個が占める決まった大きさではありません。\\ 温度と圧力を指定したときに、多数の粒子の運動から現れる体積です。\\ "
"この数値実験では、その値に近い体積を、有限個のArの運動と圧力から求められました。\\ "
"理想気体の式をゼロから証明する計算でも、実在気体の高精度な状態方程式を決める計算でもありません。"
msgstr ""
"The value 22.4 L is not a fixed size that a single atom occupies. \\ It "
"is a volume that emerges from the motion of many particles at a specified"
" temperature and pressure. \\ In this numerical experiment, we obtained a"
" volume close to that value from the motion and pressure of a finite "
"number of Ar atoms. \\ The calculation neither proves the ideal gas "
"equation from scratch nor establishes a high-precision equation of state "
"for a real gas."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:222
msgid "次の :doc:`five_gases_avogadro` では、分子の質量を変えたときの速さと圧力を比較します。"
msgstr ""
"In the next part, :doc:`five_gases_avogadro`, we compare speeds and "
"pressures as the molecular mass changes."

